{"id":"mahabharata-9-015","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":15,"title":"पञ्चदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 15 · Arjuna and Bhima rout the army","summary":{"en":"Duryodhana's troops rally around the Madra king and attack again, and Arjuna rushes against them. Yudhishthira calls for his terrible spear to kill Shalya, and the army, scattered by Arjuna, flees.","kn":"ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಮದ್ರರಾಜನ ಸುತ್ತ ಒಗ್ಗೂಡಿ ಮತ್ತೆ ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತದೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ಅವರ ಮೇಲೆ ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಲ್ಯನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲಲು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ತನ್ನ ಭಯಂಕರ ಶಕ್ತಿ ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಂದ ಚದುರಿದ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಓಡುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"दुर्योधन की सेना मद्रराज के चारों ओर जुटकर फिर आक्रमण करती है और अर्जुन उन पर टूटते हैं। युधिष्ठिर शल्य को मारने के लिए अपनी भयंकर शक्ति मँगवाते हैं, और अर्जुन से बिखरी सेना भागती है।","te":"దుర్యోధనుని సేన మద్రరాజు చుట్టూ చేరి మళ్లీ దాడి చేస్తుంది; అర్జునుడు వారిపై దూకుతాడు. శల్యుని చంపడానికి యుధిష్ఠిరుడు తన భయంకర శక్తిని తెప్పిస్తాడు; అర్జునునిచే చెదిరిన సేన పారిపోతుంది.","ta":"துரியோதனனின் படை மத்ர மன்னனைச் சுற்றித் திரண்டு மீண்டும் தாக்க, அர்ஜுனன் அவர்களை நோக்கிப் பாய்கிறான். சல்யனைக் கொல்ல யுதிஷ்டிரர் தம் கொடிய வேலை வரவழைக்க, அர்ஜுனனால் சிதறிய படை ஓடுகிறது.","ml":"മദ്രരാജാവിനു ചുറ്റും ദുര്യോധനന്റെ സേന ഒന്നിച്ചുകൂടി വീണ്ടും ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; അർജുനൻ അവർക്കുനേരെ കുതിക്കുന്നു. ശല്യനെ വധിക്കാൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ തന്റെ ഭയങ്കര കുന്തം ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; അർജുനൻ ചിതറിച്ച സേന ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.15; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः सैन्यास्तव विभो मद्रराजपुरस्कृताः ।\nपुनरभ्यद्रवन्पार्थान्वेगेन महता रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your troops, my lord, with the king of Madras in front, again charged the sons of Pritha in the battle with great speed."}},{"n":2,"text":"पीडितास्तावकाः सर्वे प्रधावन्तो रणोत्कटाः ।\nक्षणेनैव च पार्थांस्ते बहुत्वात्समलोडयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pressed hard, all your men, hot for battle, rushed on, and in a moment, by their numbers, they threw the Pandavas into turmoil."}},{"n":3,"text":"ते वध्यमानाः कुरुभिः पाण्डवा नावतस्थिरे ।\nनिवार्यमाणा भीमेन पश्यतोः कृष्णपार्थयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by the Kurus, the Pandavas could not hold their ground, though Bhima tried to hold them back while Krishna and Arjuna looked on."}},{"n":4,"text":"ततो धनंजयः क्रुद्धः कृपं सह पदानुगैः ।\nअवाकिरच्छरौघेण कृतवर्माणमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then angry Dhananjaya covered Kripa and his followers, and Kritavarman too, with floods of arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"शकुनिं सहदेवस्तु सहसैन्यमवारयत् ।\nनकुलः पार्श्वतः स्थित्वा मद्रराजमवैक्षत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sahadeva held back Shakuni together with his troops, and Nakula, standing to one side, kept watch on the king of Madras."}},{"n":6,"text":"द्रौपदेया नरेन्द्रांश्च भूयिष्ठं समवारयन् ।\nद्रोणपुत्रं च पाञ्चाल्यः शिखण्डी समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sons of Draupadi held back most of the kings, and Shikhandi, the Panchala, held back Drona's son."}},{"n":7,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु राजानं गदापाणिरवारयत् ।\nशल्यं तु सह सैन्येन कुन्तीपुत्रो युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, mace in hand, held back the king Duryodhana, and Yudhishthira, son of Kunti, held back Shalya with his army."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततः समभवद्युद्धं संसक्तं तत्र तत्र ह ।\nतावकानां परेषां च संग्रामेष्वनिवर्तिनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the fighting grew close and tangled here and there, between your men and the enemy, none of whom turned back from the battles."}},{"n":9,"text":"तत्र पश्यामहे कर्म शल्यस्यातिमहद्रणे ।\nयदेकः सर्वसैन्यानि पाण्डवानामयुध्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a very great deed of Shalya in that battle: alone, he fought all the armies of the Pandavas."}},{"n":10,"text":"व्यदृश्यत तदा शल्यो युधिष्ठिरसमीपतः ।\nरणे चन्द्रमसोऽभ्याशे शनैश्चर इव ग्रहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Near Yudhishthira then Shalya was seen in the battle like the planet Saturn near the moon."}},{"n":11,"text":"पीडयित्वा तु राजानं शरैराशीविषोपमैः ।\nअभ्यधावत्पुनर्भीमं शरवर्षैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having hurt the king with arrows like venomous snakes, he rushed again at Bhima and covered him with showers of arrows."}},{"n":12,"text":"तस्य तल्लाघवं दृष्ट्वा तथैव च कृतास्त्रताम् ।\nअपूजयन्ननीकानि परेषां तावकानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his quickness and skill with weapons, the troops of the enemy and of your side praised him."}},{"n":13,"text":"पीड्यमानास्तु शल्येन पाण्डवा भृशविक्षताः ।\nप्राद्रवन्त रणं हित्वा क्रोशमाने युधिष्ठिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Harried by Shalya, the Pandavas, badly wounded, fled from the battle while Yudhishthira called out to them."}},{"n":14,"text":"वध्यमानेष्वनीकेषु मद्रराजेन पाण्डवः ।\nअमर्षवशमापन्नो धर्मराजो युधिष्ठिरः ।\nततः पौरुषमास्थाय मद्रराजमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the divisions were being cut down by the king of Madras, Yudhishthira the Pandava, the king of dharma, was overcome by anger; then, relying on his manhood, he pressed the king of Madras."}},{"n":15,"text":"जयो वास्तु वधो वेति कृतबुद्धिर्महारथः ।\nसमाहूयाब्रवीत्सर्वान्भ्रातॄन्कृष्णं च माधवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great warrior, resolved on \"victory or death,\" called all his brothers and Krishna Madhava and said:"}},{"n":16,"text":"भीष्मो द्रोणश्च कर्णश्च ये चान्ये पृथिवीक्षितः ।\nकौरवार्थे पराक्रान्ताः संग्रामे निधनं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Bhishma, Drona, Karna and other kings, who fought valiantly for the Kauravas, have met their death in the battle.\""}},{"n":17,"text":"यथाभागं यथोत्साहं भवन्तः कृतपौरुषाः ।\nभागोऽवशिष्ट एकोऽयं मम शल्यो महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Each of you has shown his manhood according to his share and his zeal. Only one share is left to me: this great warrior Shalya.\""}},{"n":18,"text":"सोऽहमद्य युधा जेतुमाशंसे मद्रकेश्वरम् ।\nतत्र यन्मानसं मह्यं तत्सर्वं निगदामि वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"So today I hope to conquer the lord of Madra in battle. I will tell you all that is in my mind about it.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"चक्ररक्षाविमौ शूरौ मम माद्रवतीसुतौ ।\nअजेयौ वासवेनापि समरे वीरसंमतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"These two brave sons of Madri, my wheel-guards, are unconquerable even by Indra in battle, and honored as heroes.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"साध्विमौ मातुलं युद्धे क्षत्रधर्मपुरस्कृतौ ।\nमदर्थं प्रतियुध्येतां मानार्हौ सत्यसंगरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Putting the kshatriya's duty first, these two worthy of honor and true to their word should fight their maternal uncle for my sake.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"मां वा शल्यो रणे हन्ता तं वाहं भद्रमस्तु वः ।\nइति सत्यामिमां वाणीं लोकवीरा निबोधत ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Either Shalya will kill me in the battle or I will kill him; may it be well with you. Heroes of the world, know this as my true word.\""}},{"n":22,"text":"योत्स्येऽहं मातुलेनाद्य क्षत्रधर्मेण पार्थिवाः ।\nस्वयं समभिसंधाय विजयायेतराय वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Today, kings, I will fight my maternal uncle by the kshatriya's duty, determined myself on victory or the other.\""}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्य मेऽभ्यधिकं शस्त्रं सर्वोपकरणानि च ।\nसंयुञ्जन्तु रणे क्षिप्रं शास्त्रवद्रथयोजकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let the chariot-yokers, as the rules require, quickly supply me in battle with excess weapons and all equipment.\""}},{"n":24,"text":"शैनेयो दक्षिणं चक्रं धृष्टद्युम्नस्तथोत्तरम् ।\nपृष्ठगोपो भवत्वद्य मम पार्थो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let Satyaki guard the right wheel and Dhrishtadyumna the left; let Dhananjaya, son of Pritha, be my rear guard today.\""}},{"n":25,"text":"पुरःसरो ममाद्यास्तु भीमः शस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nएवमभ्यधिकः शल्याद्भविष्यामि महामृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Let Bhima, best of weapon-bearers, go before me today. So I shall be superior to Shalya in the great battle.\""}},{"n":26,"text":"एवमुक्तास्तथा चक्रुः सर्वे राज्ञः प्रियैषिणः ।\nततः प्रहर्षः सैन्यानां पुनरासीत्तदा नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"So told, all those who wished the king well did as he said, and then the troops were glad again, O king."}},{"n":27,"text":"पाञ्चालानां सोमकानां मत्स्यानां च विशेषतः ।\nप्रतिज्ञां तां च संग्रामे धर्मराजस्य पूरयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Panchalas, Somakas and especially the Matsyas, to fulfil that vow of the king of dharma in battle,"}},{"n":28,"text":"ततः शङ्खांश्च भेरीश्च शतशश्चैव पुष्करान् ।\nअवादयन्त पाञ्चालाः सिंहनादांश्च नेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"blew conches and kettledrums, and hundreds of pushkara drums, and roared lion roars."}},{"n":29,"text":"तेऽभ्यधावन्त संरब्धा मद्रराजं तरस्विनः ।\nमहता हर्षजेनाथ नादेन कुरुपुंगवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, furious and strong, they ran at the king of Madras, those bulls of the Kurus, with a great cry born of joy,"}},{"n":30,"text":"ह्रादेन गजघण्टानां शङ्खानां निनदेन च ।\nतूर्यशब्देन महता नादयन्तश्च मेदिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"with the clang of elephant bells, the blare of conches and the great sound of trumpets, making the earth ring."}},{"n":31,"text":"तान्प्रत्यगृह्णात्पुत्रस्ते मद्रराजश्च वीर्यवान् ।\nमहामेघानिव बहूञ्शैलावस्तोदयावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your son and the mighty king of Madras met them, like two mountains, the sunrise and the sunset ranges, meeting many great clouds."}},{"n":32,"text":"शल्यस्तु समरश्लाघी धर्मराजमरिंदमम् ।\nववर्ष शरवर्षेण वर्षेण मघवानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, proud of his skill in battle, showered the king of dharma, tamer of foes, with a rain of arrows like Indra with rain."}},{"n":33,"text":"तथैव कुरुराजोऽपि प्रगृह्य रुचिरं धनुः ।\nद्रोणोपदेशान्विविधान्दर्शयानो महामनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the same way the great-minded king of the Kurus took up a fine bow and displayed the many arts taught by Drona,"}},{"n":34,"text":"ववर्ष शरवर्षाणि चित्रं लघु च सुष्ठु च ।\nन चास्य विवरं कश्चिद्ददर्श चरतो रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"and rained showers of arrows, varied, quick and well aimed, and no one saw any opening as he moved in the battle."}},{"n":35,"text":"तावुभौ विविधैर्बाणैस्ततक्षाते परस्परम् ।\nशार्दूलावामिषप्रेप्सू पराक्रान्ताविवाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"They tore at each other with arrows of many kinds, like two tigers after meat, bold in the fight."}},{"n":36,"text":"भीमस्तु तव पुत्रेण रणशौण्डेन संगतः ।\nपाञ्चाल्यः सात्यकिश्चैव माद्रीपुत्रौ च पाण्डवौ ।\nशकुनिप्रमुखान्वीरान्प्रत्यगृह्णन्समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima met your son, who was proud in battle; Dhrishtadyumna, Satyaki and the two Pandava sons of Madri held off the heroes led by Shakuni on every side."}},{"n":37,"text":"तदासीत्तुमुलं युद्धं पुनरेव जयैषिणाम् ।\nतावकानां परेषां च राजन्दुर्मन्त्रिते तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then again there was a tumultuous fight between those who wished for victory, your men and the enemy, king, because of your ill counsel."}},{"n":38,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु भीमस्य शरेणानतपर्वणा ।\nचिच्छेदादिश्य संग्रामे ध्वजं हेमविभूषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, aiming in the battle, cut down the gold-adorned banner of Bhima with an arrow with bent joints."}},{"n":39,"text":"सकिङ्किणीकजालेन महता चारुदर्शनः ।\nपपात रुचिरः सिंहो भीमसेनस्य नानदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It fell, handsome with its great network of little bells, a fine lion, roaring, from Bhimasena's chariot."}},{"n":40,"text":"पुनश्चास्य धनुश्चित्रं गजराजकरोपमम् ।\nक्षुरेण शितधारेण प्रचकर्त नराधिपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king cut Bhima's bright bow too, like an elephant king's trunk, with a sharp-edged razor-arrow."}},{"n":41,"text":"स च्छिन्नधन्वा तेजस्वी रथशक्त्या सुतं तव ।\nबिभेदोरसि विक्रम्य स रथोपस्थ आविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That mighty man, his bow cut, with a chariot-lance struck your son in the chest, and he sank down onto the seat of the chariot."}},{"n":42,"text":"तस्मिन्मोहमनुप्राप्ते पुनरेव वृकोदरः ।\nयन्तुरेव शिरः कायात्क्षुरप्रेणाहरत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he was in a swoon, Bhima, the wolf-bellied, again cut the head of his charioteer from his body with a razor-arrow."}},{"n":43,"text":"हतसूता हयास्तस्य रथमादाय भारत ।\nव्यद्रवन्त दिशो राजन्हाहाकारस्तदाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bharata, his horses, their charioteer dead, took his chariot and bolted in all directions, O king, and a cry of dismay arose."}},{"n":44,"text":"तमभ्यधावत्त्राणार्थं द्रोणपुत्रो महारथः ।\nकृपश्च कृतवर्मा च पुत्रं तेऽभिपरीप्सवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son, a great warrior, ran after him to protect him, and Kripa and Kritavarman too, anxious to save your son."}},{"n":45,"text":"तस्मिन्विलुलिते सैन्ये त्रस्तास्तस्य पदानुगाः ।\nगाण्डीवधन्वा विस्फार्य धनुस्तानहनच्छरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that army was in disorder, his terrified followers were struck by the wielder of Gandiva, who stretched his bow and killed them with arrows."}},{"n":46,"text":"युधिष्ठिरस्तु मद्रेशमभ्यधावदमर्षितः ।\nस्वयं संचोदयन्नश्वान्दन्तवर्णान्मनोजवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, in anger, charged the lord of Madra, himself urging on his horses, tusk-white and swift as thought."}},{"n":47,"text":"तत्राद्भुतमपश्याम कुन्तीपुत्रे युधिष्ठिरे ।\nपुरा भूत्वा मृदुर्दान्तो यत्तदा दारुणोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There we saw a wonder in Yudhishthira, son of Kunti: he, who had been gentle and self-controlled before, then became dreadful."}},{"n":48,"text":"विवृताक्षश्च कौन्तेयो वेपमानश्च मन्युना ।\nचिच्छेद योधान्निशितैः शरैः शतसहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With eyes wide and trembling with fury, the son of Kunti cut down warriors with sharp arrows, by hundreds of thousands."}},{"n":49,"text":"यां यां प्रत्युद्ययौ सेनां तां तां ज्येष्ठः स पाण्डवः ।\nशरैरपातयद्राजन्गिरीन्वज्रैरिवोत्तमैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever army that eldest Pandava moved against, O king, he brought down with arrows as the best thunderbolts bring down mountains."}},{"n":50,"text":"साश्वसूतध्वजरथान्रथिनः पातयन्बहून् ।\nआक्रीडदेको बलवान्पवनस्तोयदानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Felling many chariot-fighters with their horses, charioteers, banners and chariots, that strong man sported alone like the wind among clouds."}},{"n":51,"text":"साश्वारोहांश्च तुरगान्पत्तींश्चैव सहस्रशः ।\nव्यपोथयत संग्रामे क्रुद्धो रुद्रः पशूनिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the battle he beat down thousands of horses with their riders and foot soldiers, like angry Rudra killing cattle."}},{"n":52,"text":"शून्यमायोधनं कृत्वा शरवर्षैः समन्ततः ।\nअभ्यद्रवत मद्रेशं तिष्ठ शल्येति चाब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having emptied the battlefield with showers of arrows all round, he charged the lord of Madra and said, \"Stand, Shalya!\""}},{"n":53,"text":"तस्य तच्चरितं दृष्ट्वा संग्रामे भीमकर्मणः ।\nवित्रेसुस्तावकाः सर्वे शल्यस्त्वेनं समभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that deed of his in the battle, he of terrible acts, all your men were terrified, but Shalya came against him."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततस्तौ तु सुसंरब्धौ प्रध्माप्य सलिलोद्भवौ ।\nसमाहूय तदान्योन्यं भर्त्सयन्तौ समीयतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two furious ones, blowing their conches, challenging each other and rebuking each other, came together."}},{"n":55,"text":"शल्यस्तु शरवर्षेण युधिष्ठिरमवाकिरत् ।\nमद्रराजं च कौन्तेयः शरवर्षैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya covered Yudhishthira with a rain of arrows, and the son of Kunti covered the king of Madras with rains of arrows."}},{"n":56,"text":"व्यदृश्येतां तदा राजन्कङ्कपत्रिभिराहवे ।\nउद्भिन्नरुधिरौ शूरौ मद्रराजयुधिष्ठिरौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, the two heroes, Shalya and Yudhishthira, were seen in the fight, bleeding from wounds made by heron-feathered arrows."}},{"n":57,"text":"पुष्पिताविव रेजाते वने शल्मलिकिंशुकौ ।\nदीप्यमानौ महात्मानौ प्राणयोर्युद्धदुर्मदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two great-souled men, blazing, wild in the fight with their lives at stake, shone like a flowering silk-cotton and kimshuka tree in a forest."}},{"n":58,"text":"दृष्ट्वा सर्वाणि सैन्यानि नाध्यवस्यंस्तयोर्जयम् ।\nहत्वा मद्राधिपं पार्थो भोक्ष्यतेऽद्य वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them, all the armies could not decide which would win: \"Will Partha kill the lord of Madra and enjoy the earth today,"}},{"n":59,"text":"शल्यो वा पाण्डवं हत्वा दद्याद्दुर्योधनाय गाम् ।\nइतीव निश्चयो नाभूद्योधानां तत्र भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"or will Shalya kill the Pandava and give the earth to Duryodhana?\" No such certainty arose in the warriors there, Bharata."}},{"n":60,"text":"प्रदक्षिणमभूत्सर्वं धर्मराजस्य युध्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet everything went auspiciously, to the right, for the king of dharma as he fought."}},{"n":61,"text":"ततः शरशतं शल्यो मुमोचाशु युधिष्ठिरे ।\nधनुश्चास्य शिताग्रेण बाणेन निरकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shalya quickly shot a hundred arrows at Yudhishthira, and cut his bow with a sharp-pointed arrow."}},{"n":62,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय शल्यं शरशतैस्त्रिभिः ।\nअविध्यत्कार्मुकं चास्य क्षुरेण निरकृन्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking another bow, Yudhishthira pierced Shalya with three hundred arrows and cut his bow with a razor-arrow."}},{"n":63,"text":"अथास्य निजघानाश्वांश्चतुरो नतपर्वभिः ।\nद्वाभ्यामथ शिताग्राभ्यामुभौ च पार्ष्णिसारथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shalya killed his four horses with arrows with bent joints and with two sharp-pointed arrows the two rear guards of his chariot."}},{"n":64,"text":"ततोऽस्य दीप्यमानेन पीतेन निशितेन च ।\nप्रमुखे वर्तमानस्य भल्लेनापाहरद्ध्वजम् ।\nततः प्रभग्नं तत्सैन्यं दौर्योधनमरिंदम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as Shalya stood in front, Yudhishthira cut his banner with a bright, yellow, sharp broad-headed arrow; and then, tamer of foes, Duryodhana's army broke and fled."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततो मद्राधिपं द्रौणिरभ्यधावत्तथाकृतम् ।\nआरोप्य चैनं स्वरथं त्वरमाणः प्रदुद्रुवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Drona's son ran to the lord of Madra, who was in this state, set him on his own chariot, and fled in haste."}},{"n":66,"text":"मुहूर्तमिव तौ गत्वा नर्दमाने युधिष्ठिरे ।\nस्थित्वा ततो मद्रपतिरन्यं स्यन्दनमास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After going for a moment, while Yudhishthira roared, the lord of Madra halted and mounted another chariot,"}},{"n":67,"text":"विधिवत्कल्पितं शुभ्रं महाम्बुदनिनादिनम् ।\nसज्जयन्त्रोपकरणं द्विषतां रोमहर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"properly fitted out, shining, rumbling like a great cloud, supplied with machines and gear, a thing to make enemies' hair stand on end."}}]}]}